#### 1. Access Control Issues

**Vulnerability Type:** Access control issues

**Severity:** High

**Affected Code Location:** `transferToken`, `mintToken`, `burnToken`, `setLock`, `frozenAccount`

**Description of the Issue:** The chaincode does not enforce proper access control. Any user can call these functions without proper authorization. For example, a user can transfer tokens, mint new tokens, or set the lock status without being authorized to do so.

**Recommended Fix:** Implement access control checks to ensure that only authorized users can perform certain actions. This can be done by checking the identity of the caller and verifying their permissions.

